{
  "caveats": [
    "One machine, one process, CPython's built-in big integers. A production deployment would use a GMP-backed modular exponentiation and should expect roughly an order of magnitude better on every RSA row.",
    "Accumulator verification is not faster than Merkle verification per record and this benchmark shows that. The saving is in verifier state and proof bandwidth, and in answering absence and completeness, which Merkle proofs cannot answer at any price.",
    "The modulus here is locally generated with known factors so the benchmark is reproducible. Timings are unaffected; the security argument is not the same one a deployment would make."
